# LeakSanitizer suppressions for kmx-aio.
#
# Read automatically by script/feature/common.sh whenever an ASan build runs, and only then: LSan takes
# its options from LSAN_OPTIONS, which is set only when the address sanitizer is actually active.
#
# A suppression belongs here when the allocation is genuinely not ours to free - a library that
# allocates once per process and hands ownership to no one, most often. Anything the library itself
# allocates is a leak worth fixing, not worth suppressing. Each entry should say which library it
# covers and why, so that a later toolchain or dependency update can tell whether it still applies.
#
# The syntax is one "leak:<substring>" per line, matched against function or library names in the
# allocation stack, for example:
#
#     leak:libcrypto.so
#     leak:vsomeip_v3::runtime::get
#
# No suppressions are active: every leak the current test suite reports is one to look at.
